{
 "_about": "Built-in effort per (agent type, model alias) for /override-agent (agent_guard.py). INITIAL DEFAULTS from rule v1, to be re-derived from measured data (the Bayesian/Pareto limits jobs); a change applies to overrides set after it, never to one already set in a running session (the command stores the resolved level).",
 "rule": "v1 (2026-10-03): base = the agent's frontmatter effort, its level as tuned on its own model. Same or stronger model (tiers sonnet < opus < fable): base. A model weaker than the agent's own (opus agent on sonnet): one level up, at most xhigh (max is never chosen by the rule). No haiku column (2026-10-05): the stack runs no Haiku, so /override-agent offers sonnet, opus and fable. At use the level is clamped to what the resolved model accepts (models).",
 "version": 1,
 "models": {
  "_source": "Claude Code 2.1.287 effort predicates (supportedEffortLevels; max_effort / xhigh_effort checks): no max or xhigh on claude-3-*, claude-opus-4-0/4-1/4-5, claude-sonnet-4-0/4-5, claude-haiku-4-5; no xhigh on claude-opus-4-6, claude-sonnet-4-6; other current models (the 5.x family, claude-fable-5, claude-fable-5-1) low..max. Which old models accept no effort at all is unverified: assumed claude-3-* and claude-haiku-4-5.",
